WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:08.480
<b>The Ghost of Laplace</b>

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.220
Message from ECOAS. "Object ball placed in pyramid spot," sir.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.860
Attention! Initiate Phase 3.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:25.240
This ship will now breach enemy airspace at maximum combat speed

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:30.040
and attack the Neo Zeon stronghold with our hyper mega particle cannon.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:33.080
This one strike will determine the success of the mission.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.110
I expect all crew members to do their utmost.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.030
Nashiri Team is proceeding to Phase 2.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.830
Right. Now proceeding to target retrieval point.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.750
Once Banagher Links' retrieval has been confirmed,

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.500
we'll join with Team Alpha to recapture the Gundam.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.210
This will be a hit-and-fade operation.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:34.720
After the advance team has separated Palau's four asteroids,

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.720
we'll fire the hyper mega particle cannon to seal off the military port.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.510
The plan is to retrieve Banagher Links and the Unicorn while this is going on.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.450
I take it that you will attack only Palau's military facilities?

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.600
Yes. The Federation has spies there, too.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.750
We wouldn't come up with a plan that would damage the residential block.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.950
That look on your face says you'll go back

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.320
and inform your people by yourself if you have to.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.290
You'll just have to take my word for it.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.470
We may be at our closest approach, but it's still two days to Earth.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.660
I could only scrounge up the bare minimum of food and water.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.570
I'm prepared to do what I must.

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:28.310
What's going on, Mr. Ensign?

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.560
Are you helping the prisoner escape? Where are you taking that girl?

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.190
Please, just wait. I can't tell you exactly what's going on, but-

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.530
Ensign Riddhe!

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.880
We're going to Earth.

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:46.620
Just because the Ensign is coming with me does not mean in any way

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.660
that he is betraying the Federation, or you and your friends.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:56.130
I realized that in these circumstances, there is something that only I can do.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.230
As did Ensign Riddhe.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:00.920
Like I could believe anything that the Zeons' princess says!

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.860
It's of vital importance.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:10.060
To prevent this from escalating further, this is all that I can do right now.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.620
Ms. Micott...

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.320
This doesn't mean I've forgiven you.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.530
You owe me one.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.330
Go fulfill your responsibilities on Earth as best you can.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.060
Dad!

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.840
What's this about sudden orders?!

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.310
I don't understand; you just came home!

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.890
It's all right. Don't you worry.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.350
Look after your mother and siblings.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.770
O-Okay...

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.910
The kid made a run for it, huh?

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.320
I'm sorry, sir.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.830
He won't be able to leave Palau.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:59.040
Still, I had no idea he had it in him.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.220
Explosion flashes observed in Palau's connecting shafts!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.730
Entering enemy airspace momentarily!

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.710
Engines off! Begin inertial coasting!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.720
Transfer all power to the hyper mega particle cannon!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.630
Disperse Minovsky particles at combat density!

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.740
Mobile suit corps, launch in sequence!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.390
This is insanity!

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.920
Hyper mega particle cannon, ready to fire!

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:09.360
Commence attack when we reach the planned point!

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.570
Remind friendly suits to stay clear of our line of fire!

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.600
Roger that!

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.310
Bridge to all suits.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:18.100
We will now fire the hyper mega particle cannon.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.500
Time to reach point, 48, 47, 46...

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.050
All deployed mobile suits,

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.500
evacuate field of fire immediately!

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.080
45...

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.160
44...

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.160
43...

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.420
42...

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.330
41...

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.330
40...

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.430
39...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.500
38...

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.590
37...

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:33.720
36...

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.930
35...

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:35.700
34...

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.520
24...

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.600
23...

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.630
22...

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:49.770
21...

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:50.690
20...

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:51.690
19...

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:52.780
18...

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:53.850
17...

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:08.920
Four!

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:09.990
Three!

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:10.960
Two!

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:11.930
One!

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.410
Fire!

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.900
Give them the slip! I'm on my way to get you!

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.840
Tikva!

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:50.900
Mom!

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.990
Two minutes beyond scheduled time.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.610
No signals detected from target.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.920
What the hell are you doing, Banagher?

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.410
What do you mean, the bay is blocked?!

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:37.890
I can't get through to the Captain! How do things look outside?!

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.750
The 14th space gate... That's it!

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.200
What are you doing here?

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.910
It'll take more than retrieving me to end this operation.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:07.860
We can't stay here... Not me.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:09.570
Or you.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.410
Juliet 005, laser signal terminated!

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:32.730
Multiple trailing enemy suits! Friendly suits are being surrounded!

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:35.630
Send in our own escort suits as reinforcements! Take the ship in, too!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:38.790
Begin anti-air fire! Release dummy asteroids!

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.050
Any word from ECOAS?

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.840
Communications are still dark.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.140
We walked right into it!

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:48.290
They anticipated what we were going to do!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.630
Captain! New comm signal detected from Palau!

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.400
Is it ECOAS?

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.210
No, this is...

00:09:58.190 --> 00:09:59.380
...the Gundam!

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.600
They're not attacking with a large force?

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.770
The Nahel Argama is coming!

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.110
What?

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:20.700
Come on, hurry!

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.500
Please, let me go!

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.360
If you don't, the Federation will never pull back!

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.190
Do you people want to turn Palau into a battlefield?!

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:50.710
Why?!

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.030
Why did this have to happen?

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:05.710
We walked into a trap?

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.380
Please go.

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:09.840
You ought to carry out your duties.

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.100
It's your forces that I'll be fighting.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:16.960
That is my problem. Be true to your own heart.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.660
If you turn your back on them now, you will regret it for the rest of your life.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.400
You got me.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:28.060
I'll break away once our forces leave. Sorry, but tag along with me until then.

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:29.080
Right.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.630
That should give you an excuse! Now go home!

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:57.920
Here comes another.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.120
The Unicorn Gundam!

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.050
But who is...

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:07.780
A new Federation model?

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.320
Banagher! Banagher Links, that's you, isn't it?

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.270
Audrey? Audrey, is that you?

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.940
You're all right, Banagher! It's me. Minev...

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:26.280
It's Audrey Burne. I'm so glad that you're safe.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:30.090
What are you doing here? Are you piloting that suit?

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:32.410
I'd like to know what you are doing in the Gundam.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.590
What happened to the ECOAS team?

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:36.120
Who are you?

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:42.550
Ensign Riddhe Marcenas. You caught my good-luck charm, remember?

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:44.630
Ensign Riddhe?

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.010
Banagher!

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.100
I'm delivering her to Earth.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.180
To Earth?

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:52.890
I've given it a great deal of thought.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.700
Ensign Riddhe's father is Assemblyman Ronan Marcenas

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:58.770
of the Federation Central Assembly.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:01.950
He's a central figure of Spacenoid policy.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:05.540
I will meet with him and tell him everything that has happened.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:09.760
As heir to the Zabi bloodline, I want to resolve this situation peace-

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.220
Hey, slow down a second!

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:14.470
This is a lot to take in quickly, so I understand your confusion.

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:17.790
It won't be easy to do, but we want to find the best way out of this.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:19.960
You should return to the Nahel Argama.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:23.130
With you and the Unicorn back, the Federation will withdraw its forces.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:40.330
I'll see this through and deliver Mineva... No, Audrey.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:45.320
This Delta Plus is capable of unassisted atmospheric reentry.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.490
Audrey, tell me one thing.

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:51.670
Is this what you want?

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.580
Yes. I believe so.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:57.260
I understand. Ensign Riddhe.

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.270
I'll take your word as a man.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.130
Take good care of Audrey.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:08.510
He sure knows how to motivate someone.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:20.310
We used too much propellant. We'll use that mass driver.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:21.540
Ensign? Banagher is-

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:22.970
I know.

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:26.470
This is between two men. Please stay out of it.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.430
Did he give up?

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:48.210
The quad-wing, huh?

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:53.820
What the...

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:02.100
Securing the suit has top priority, as long as the cockpit core is intact.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:06.540
I guess no war is ever justified, is it?

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:17.760
That's you, isn't it, Ms. Marida?

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:19.260
How did he...?

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:21.290
It's Banagher! Banagher Links!

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:23.750
If that's you, Ms. Marida, you have to listen!

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:30.780
Surrender, Banagher Links. If you don't, I'll fry your cockpit.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.310
What are you doing in there?

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:34.740
Who I am doesn't matter.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:39.310
Right now, you and I are just combat units called pilots.

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:41.110
Cut your main generator right now, and-

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:41.910
Even so!

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.120
Even so, you're still Ms. Marida!

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.900
That's how I sensed you. That's how I knew it was you.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:51.110
Palau is your team's home, right?

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:55.340
If they get the Unicorn back, the Federation will leave this place!

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:57.460
That's just an enemy's rationalization.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:16:00.840
Audrey's here, too! She came to put an end to the fighting!

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.830
The Princess? Where is she?

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:06.220
Please, just think about stopping the fighting for now.

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:08.300
Everyone who lives at Palau,

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.340
even Mr. Gilboa's family, might get caught in the crossfire!

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:14.600
If you surrender and tell me where the Princess is,

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.300
we'll withdraw our forces, too.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:20.320
Look at yourself! You say you only want to end the fighting,

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.820
but you're thinking from the Federation's point of view!

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:25.030
I'm not! I'm not on their side, Ms. Marida!

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:27.030
You people are too single-minded!

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:29.000
That's why Audrey says not to give the Box to you!

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.360
Like I said, just an enemy's rationalization!

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:38.260
You stubborn idiot!

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:45.430
Gundam!

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:56.430
NT-D activation confirmed. Enemy has engaged the kshatriya.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:17:01.280
Our psycho-monitor reception might force us to come out from behind Palau.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:03.740
keep a close eye out for enemy ships, too.

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.310
A job fit for a cyber-Newtype, huh?

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:09.190
Why are you leaving Marida to fight alone?

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:12.250
This is a job that only the Lieutenant can do.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.420
The only way to activate the NT-D

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:17.360
is to get him to fight someone who could be a Newtype.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:21.380
We've installed a psycho-monitor aboard the Unicorn Gundam.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:26.380
We'll intercept any Box data disclosed by the activation of the NT-D.

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:29.230
Since we cannot analyze the La+ Program itself,

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.800
the fastest way is to gradually break the seals on the system.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.650
To accomplish that, we used the Federation's inside man

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:41.070
to lead that boy Banagher to the Unicorn.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:44.020
I regret leaving you in the dark, Captain.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.120
But Marida is a-

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.900
Yes, I know.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:50.490
A cyber-Newtype can't be said to be a pure Newtype.

00:17:50.490 --> 00:17:54.150
Then again, Captain, what exactly is a "pure" Newtype?

00:17:54.610 --> 00:17:56.620
No one has the answer to that.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:01.250
What we need at the moment is a "phenomenon" that will trigger the NT-D.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:05.080
That Gundam has yet to show its true colors.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:09.250
We're going to have Lt. Marida draw out its true nature.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:13.560
Funnels!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.580
Don't you recognize me?

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.920
Who are you?

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:05.650
Is it that boy who's doing that?

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:07.600
Not precisely.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:10.270
Right now, the pilot is just a processing mechanism

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:13.170
for converting received psycho-waves into hostility.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.040
Then what is it that's driving that Gundam?

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:19.990
The NT-D. Newtype Destroyer System.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:24.990
If it identifies the enemy as a Newtype, the suit's limiters are disengaged.

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:28.760
It's a hunting machine that combines the paranormal interface

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:33.620
of the psycho-frame and the power to take control of an enemy's psycommu weapons.

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:37.670
No ordinary human could possibly handle a machine like that.

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:39.340
Indeed they cannot.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:43.090
Which is why you need a cyber-Newtype, a literally enhanced human.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:46.850
The day that Newtypes can be destroyed

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:50.230
by a product of technology is the day they will be consigned to history.

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:53.120
Just as the Universal Century is about to mark its hundredth year,

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.770
the UC Project was aptly named, indeed.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:10.870
In other words, you threw Marida out there to be bait, eh?

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:14.170
Ple Twelve. That is her name.

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:19.630
She is an artificial Newtype, created via cloning and genetic modification.

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.420
The 12th prototype.

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:00.600
Master, you died? Why?

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:02.780
What should I do, Master?

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:05.850
What a smelly girl!

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:08.060
What will you do with a child like this?

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:11.190
Some of our clients are into that sort of thing, right?

00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:14.060
Starting today, I'm your Master.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.060
But she's so young!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.560
You've had that dead weight removed, right? Come on!

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:22.120
What do you mean? What army?

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.860
If you're some kind of Zeon fugitive, I'm calling the pol-

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:27.780
That's enough.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.320
I'm sorry.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:47.400
This is... This is all too sad.

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:50.550
Kindness alone can't save people.

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:54.530
It can't erase sin or wash away the impurities.

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:58.310
But even so...

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:09.840
Roger that.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:13.450
We'd like to observe the inspection of the captured suit, as well.

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:14.100
Over and out.

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:19.500
It almost looked as if that quad-wing was intentionally made to fight alone.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:24.500
I hope nobody got it into their heads to rig it with a bomb.

00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:27.100
I doubt they'd need to resort to such a roundabout method

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:29.860
to take out just the Nahel Argama.

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:33.800
On the other hand, it's possible that the boy was allowed to escape.

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:37.770
I don't want to think that all this was for nothing.

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:40.940
Of course not.

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:55.530
Banagher...

00:22:57.290 --> 00:22:59.210
Looks like it's over.

00:22:59.210 --> 00:23:02.390
It looks like the Gundam has been taken aboard the Nahel Argama.

00:23:02.390 --> 00:23:03.750
That quad-wing, too.

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:07.610
I'll probably be designated as killed in action.

00:23:08.300 --> 00:23:10.510
All we can do now is forge ahead.

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:13.300
Both you... and me.

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:19.230
The NZ-666 kshatriya.

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:22.350
Judging from the model number, it's probably made by Neo Zeon.

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:26.170
There's a psycho-frame installed around the cockpit,

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:27.750
but it's an old type.

00:23:27.750 --> 00:23:31.070
I bet they repurposed a prototype that was supplied

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:33.530
by Anaheim back during Char's rebellion.

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:36.300
Captain Otto?

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:40.590
You say that only Granada on the moon

00:23:40.590 --> 00:23:42.930
has psycho-frame manufacturing facilities?

00:23:42.930 --> 00:23:43.850
Yes, sir.

00:23:43.850 --> 00:23:46.930
Since development of the technology was officially halted,

00:23:46.930 --> 00:23:50.020
they're completely responsible for it, including maintaining its secrecy.

00:23:50.020 --> 00:23:51.930
Why was it halted?

00:23:51.930 --> 00:23:55.090
I hear it was because there were just too many unknowns.

00:23:55.510 --> 00:23:59.360
Even with the Unicorn, it looks like the exposed psycho-frame

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:02.810
is glowing when the NT-D activates and the armor separates, right?

00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:07.440
We don't know why it glows, and we're the ones who built it.

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:11.300
And sometimes that glow can be converted into physical energy.

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:15.070
Um... I didn't see any of the combat records,

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:18.700
but it certainly was a one-sided fight, wasn't it?

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:22.550
Captain! Message from sickbay.

00:24:22.550 --> 00:24:24.330
The prisoner's vitals have stabilized.

00:24:25.500 --> 00:24:27.060
Aside from her external injuries,

00:24:27.060 --> 00:24:30.470
she appears to be rather weak, so it's still too soon to question her.

00:24:30.470 --> 00:24:34.840
What are all these scars from burns and lacerations all over her body?

00:24:37.010 --> 00:24:42.100
From what Dr. Hasan says, her reproductive system is also...

00:24:43.690 --> 00:24:46.320
In the closing days of the First Neo Zeon War,

00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:49.440
a Newtype Corps made up of clones was sent into battle,

00:24:49.440 --> 00:24:52.000
but they were supposed to have all been wiped out.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:56.320
But one of them survived, and this is what became of her, huh?

00:24:57.570 --> 00:24:59.750
We'll leave her questioning to Headquarters.

00:24:59.750 --> 00:25:01.080
Understood.

00:25:06.040 --> 00:25:08.050
I hope that this is the last-

00:25:08.050 --> 00:25:10.710
Detour we'll have to make? I hope so, too.

00:25:11.130 --> 00:25:13.400
I don't think that will be necessary.

00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:15.900
She's a cyber-Newtype, isn't she?

00:25:15.900 --> 00:25:18.530
If she doesn't get her medication, won't she go berserk?

00:25:18.530 --> 00:25:22.610
She's the type that was genetically designed from the ground up,

00:25:22.610 --> 00:25:24.740
so there's no need to suppress her immune response.

00:25:24.740 --> 00:25:26.020
But she-

00:25:26.020 --> 00:25:29.910
Her emotional state also seems stable, and besides, her injuries are severe.

00:25:29.910 --> 00:25:33.210
As a doctor, I can't consent to putting her in a straitjacket.

00:25:33.210 --> 00:25:35.870
But she's a Neo Zeon, remember?

00:25:35.870 --> 00:25:38.130
She might even try to hurt you, Doctor!

00:25:38.130 --> 00:25:40.120
Ms. Marida would never do that!

00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:43.040
Banagher... I didn't know you were there.

00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:44.750
How do you feel?

00:25:46.080 --> 00:25:48.210
How can you put an injured person in a straitjacket?

00:25:48.190 --> 00:25:50.690
This is none of your concern.

00:25:50.690 --> 00:25:54.270
Why would you do that? Ms. Marida's an officer.

00:25:54.270 --> 00:25:57.810
There are rules that govern the treatment of prisoners, aren't there?

00:25:57.810 --> 00:25:59.730
The Sleeves are terrorists.

00:25:59.730 --> 00:26:02.000
Even if she's an officer, she's still a criminal.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:03.080
But she's-

00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:06.060
Were you brainwashed at Palau or something?

00:26:06.060 --> 00:26:08.740
She's the pilot of that quad-wing!

00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:12.060
She's the person responsible for all the destruction at your own colony.

00:26:12.520 --> 00:26:15.900
And there's no telling how many of our people have been killed by her.

00:26:18.320 --> 00:26:21.840
But... If you start out making assumptions like that, you'll-

00:26:21.840 --> 00:26:25.790
We'll put her under guard. Please notify us when you move her.

00:26:26.200 --> 00:26:27.410
Roger that.

00:26:30.790 --> 00:26:35.670
Think about it. After all, even Ensign Riddhe didn't come back.

00:26:36.340 --> 00:26:38.570
What are cyber-Newtypes, anyway?

00:26:38.570 --> 00:26:41.020
The product of a delusion.

00:26:41.020 --> 00:26:43.800
That one might be able to create Newtypes artificially.

00:26:44.390 --> 00:26:46.450
To make a long story short, that was the sophistry they used

00:26:46.450 --> 00:26:49.810
to violate their ethics so they could create human weapons.

00:26:53.320 --> 00:26:55.200
You know the basic Newtype concept?

00:26:55.200 --> 00:26:57.660
Yes. It says that when humanity moved into space,

00:26:57.660 --> 00:27:00.170
we'd become able to understand each other without misconceptions.

00:27:00.170 --> 00:27:01.910
That's right.

00:27:01.910 --> 00:27:07.160
But if we all became like that, wars ought to become a thing of the past...

00:27:08.830 --> 00:27:11.290
Somebody once said that the reason

00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:14.130
mankind's wars never end was because we're stuck

00:27:14.130 --> 00:27:16.840
on the threshold of a new stage of evolution.

00:27:17.670 --> 00:27:20.970
If there really is a chance for us to become Newtypes,

00:27:20.970 --> 00:27:23.890
he said cyber-Newtype research should be allowed.

00:27:24.390 --> 00:27:27.140
If we leave evolution to Mother Nature,

00:27:27.140 --> 00:27:30.650
humanity will kill itself off first.

00:27:30.650 --> 00:27:33.070
I think that's a sad way of looking at things.

00:27:33.070 --> 00:27:36.210
I agree. That's why we have to work at understanding each other

00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:39.400
with the abilities we have right now, limited as they are.

00:27:43.450 --> 00:27:45.660
Our roles have reversed, I see.

00:27:49.950 --> 00:27:51.710
Don't stare at me like that.

00:27:52.540 --> 00:27:56.350
It's all a bit hazy. How did all that happen?

00:27:56.350 --> 00:27:58.850
You must have been swallowed up by the machine.

00:27:58.850 --> 00:28:01.100
A psycommu backflow.

00:28:01.100 --> 00:28:05.180
You think you're controlling it, but it suddenly starts controlling you.

00:28:06.350 --> 00:28:09.180
I sensed powerful negative intent.

00:28:09.180 --> 00:28:12.730
That was probably the instinct of the system embedded in the Gundam.

00:28:13.230 --> 00:28:15.600
To seek out Newtypes and destroy them.

00:28:16.110 --> 00:28:19.230
Even if those Newtypes are artificial ones.

00:28:19.730 --> 00:28:24.080
A machine doesn't have the capability to discern natural from artificial.

00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:25.780
But people are another story.

00:28:26.570 --> 00:28:28.500
They can sense the difference.

00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:29.450
But even you...

00:28:29.910 --> 00:28:31.950
I have a Master.

00:28:33.620 --> 00:28:39.630
Even if I was created artificially, my entire being is devoted to him.

00:28:40.130 --> 00:28:45.300
I hope for what he hopes for, and I oppose what he opposes.

00:28:46.260 --> 00:28:51.620
But that's a curse, killing yourself bit by bit like that.

00:28:51.620 --> 00:28:53.730
I saw inside you.

00:28:54.350 --> 00:28:57.230
You and I might be two of a kind.

00:28:57.770 --> 00:28:59.570
What do you mean by that?

00:29:00.940 --> 00:29:04.780
If I don't look at it that way, losing to you would be humiliating.

00:29:04.780 --> 00:29:06.960
Still, the Gundam stopped.

00:29:06.960 --> 00:29:12.870
Your will... the foundation inside you forced the system into submission.

00:29:12.870 --> 00:29:14.250
Foundation?

00:29:14.250 --> 00:29:18.790
Those like me don't have that. It's what lets us merge with machines.

00:29:19.280 --> 00:29:19.900
Ms. Marid-

00:29:19.900 --> 00:29:21.130
Never mind me.

00:29:23.260 --> 00:29:27.050
Banagher, no matter what sort of realities you're forced to confront,

00:29:27.050 --> 00:29:30.020
keep saying, "Even so..."

00:29:30.020 --> 00:29:31.930
Never lose sight of who you are.

00:29:33.270 --> 00:29:35.560
That's the foundation of who you are.

00:29:35.560 --> 00:29:40.490
The power that awakens that other system,

00:29:40.490 --> 00:29:42.860
the one sleeping in that Gundam, it...

00:29:43.990 --> 00:29:47.030
Laplace's Box was entrusted to it so it could-

00:29:50.280 --> 00:29:50.970
Ms. Marida!

00:29:51.490 --> 00:29:52.250
Ms. Marida!

00:29:52.250 --> 00:29:53.240
What's wrong?

00:30:07.220 --> 00:30:09.340
Banagher, not happy.

00:30:14.060 --> 00:30:16.560
Looks like the Captain and his officers are keeping it secret

00:30:17.560 --> 00:30:20.120
that the Zeons' princess disappeared.

00:30:20.650 --> 00:30:25.750
I just wish we could tell Ensign Mihiro that Ensign Riddhe is alive.

00:30:25.750 --> 00:30:27.420
I didn't know they were an item.

00:30:27.420 --> 00:30:29.340
An item, an item!

00:30:27.990 --> 00:30:29.340
I'm not really sure, but still.

00:30:29.780 --> 00:30:32.290
I wonder if she made it to Earth all right?

00:30:32.290 --> 00:30:34.370
He's with her, so she'll be fine.

00:30:35.120 --> 00:30:37.450
You don't really seem like yourself.

00:30:39.040 --> 00:30:42.000
You didn't use to be this cool-headed about her.

00:31:03.420 --> 00:31:06.070
Begging your pardon, sir!

00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:15.630
Master, we've just received an urgent communique from the military.

00:31:15.630 --> 00:31:17.450
Young Master Riddhe has...

00:31:20.710 --> 00:31:23.500
Princess Mineva has gone down to Earth?

00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:26.340
The intel comes from a sympathizer within the Federation Government.

00:31:26.340 --> 00:31:30.600
He says a mobile suit used Assembly privilege to cross their defensive lines.

00:31:30.600 --> 00:31:32.270
She was likely aboard.

00:31:32.270 --> 00:31:34.050
You don't think it was a diversion?

00:31:34.050 --> 00:31:35.850
The Mock Trojan Horse's position?

00:31:35.850 --> 00:31:38.740
Approaching geosynchronous orbit, sir.

00:31:38.740 --> 00:31:42.160
As I thought. So, they're headed for the designated coordinates, are they?

00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:45.160
I believe this time we'll chance upon something.

00:31:45.160 --> 00:31:48.690
It's far too perfect a place to break the La+ seal.

00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:51.650
The klimt.

00:31:51.630 --> 00:31:55.590
A shuttle used by the Vist Foundation to transport works of art, eh?

00:31:55.590 --> 00:31:58.300
They're just doing an orbital sightseeing flight

00:31:58.300 --> 00:32:00.080
above the equator without even accelerating.

00:32:00.080 --> 00:32:04.670
If we're assuming that they're meeting with someone, it must be with...

00:32:05.190 --> 00:32:09.100
Whatever their objective is, if they're planning an orbital rendezvous,

00:32:09.100 --> 00:32:10.570
it'll leave them vulnerable.

00:32:10.570 --> 00:32:12.160
Do we attack, sir?

00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:15.050
We'll be scraping atmosphere. Can we pull it off?

00:32:15.050 --> 00:32:16.320
We'll sure try.

00:32:16.320 --> 00:32:18.390
Laplace's Box notwithstanding,

00:32:18.390 --> 00:32:22.180
we can't leave Marida to stew aboard the Mock Trojan Horse, can we?

00:32:22.560 --> 00:32:24.920
Flaste, the helm's yours!

00:32:24.920 --> 00:32:28.980
W-Wait! Are you sure, Captain?

00:32:33.990 --> 00:32:35.950
I suppose he's right.

00:32:38.870 --> 00:32:43.080
The Nahel Argama will conduct an inspection of the coordinate airspace.

00:32:43.080 --> 00:32:45.850
Before the Unicorn is shipped off to Luna II,

00:32:45.850 --> 00:32:49.060
information regarding the key to Laplace's Box will be-

00:32:49.060 --> 00:32:52.560
You aren't looking well. Is there a problem?

00:32:52.560 --> 00:32:57.760
No... It's just that after all these battles, the men are exhausted.

00:32:58.140 --> 00:33:03.930
Well... I was wondering if this matter should have been left to another unit.

00:33:04.440 --> 00:33:07.650
You almost look as if you've become attached to them.

00:33:08.020 --> 00:33:10.730
Once you've landed on Earth, feel free to relax a while.

00:33:11.110 --> 00:33:12.150
Landed on Earth?

00:33:12.650 --> 00:33:15.360
I've chartered a transport.

00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:18.490
Use it to take the cyber-Newtype who's being held prisoner

00:33:18.490 --> 00:33:21.050
aboard the Nahel Argama to Augusta in North America.

00:33:21.050 --> 00:33:23.160
Augusta?

00:33:23.540 --> 00:33:24.760
Right.

00:33:24.760 --> 00:33:26.760
The labs there have been shut down,

00:33:26.760 --> 00:33:30.210
but I'm told that the facilities needed for readjustments are still there.

00:33:30.210 --> 00:33:32.340
What do you have in mind?

00:33:32.960 --> 00:33:37.020
If Grandfather had simply told me the location of the Box,

00:33:37.020 --> 00:33:40.680
I wouldn't have to resort to such underhanded methods.

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:46.780
I don't know what Grandfather and Cardeas' goal was,

00:33:46.780 --> 00:33:50.060
but if the Box is lost, so are the Foundation's fortunes.

00:33:50.610 --> 00:33:53.200
There is activity within the Federation Government

00:33:53.200 --> 00:33:56.320
to try to gain the Box for itself in anticipation of that loss.

00:33:57.070 --> 00:34:00.710
This is no time to let petty sympathies get the better of you.

00:34:00.710 --> 00:34:04.450
Laplace's Box is our very lifeline.

00:34:05.080 --> 00:34:08.250
I'm counting on you, Alberto.

00:34:08.230 --> 00:34:09.670
I won't do it!

00:34:09.960 --> 00:34:12.380
That wasn't a request.

00:34:12.380 --> 00:34:17.050
If the Unicorn is piloted through the coordinates given by the La+ Program,

00:34:17.050 --> 00:34:20.070
there's a high probability that another seal on the program will be broken.

00:34:20.600 --> 00:34:22.320
I'll ride with you.

00:34:22.320 --> 00:34:26.060
I want you to take the suit to the appropriate coordinates.

00:34:26.060 --> 00:34:27.200
That's an order.

00:34:27.200 --> 00:34:30.940
You saw it, right? You saw what happened to it at Palau, didn't you?

00:34:33.940 --> 00:34:37.820
I'm not a soldier, so I shouldn't have to take orders from you.

00:34:37.820 --> 00:34:41.490
No, you aren't obliged to obey me. But you do have a responsibility.

00:34:41.910 --> 00:34:44.870
You've intervened in battle situations three times now.

00:34:45.540 --> 00:34:47.680
With a powerful weapon.

00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:50.000
Lives may have been saved because of you,

00:34:50.960 --> 00:34:53.040
but lives were lost, too.

00:34:54.670 --> 00:35:00.610
You're already interfering in the destinies of a lot of people, friend and foe alike.

00:35:00.610 --> 00:35:03.110
You need to take responsibility for that.

00:35:03.110 --> 00:35:04.470
How do I do that?

00:35:04.850 --> 00:35:06.680
By seeing this through.

00:35:07.680 --> 00:35:09.950
keep fighting until I die, is that it?

00:35:09.950 --> 00:35:13.370
Or am I supposed to stay on this crazy treasure hunt to the bitter end?

00:35:13.370 --> 00:35:15.290
Think that over for yourself.

00:35:15.290 --> 00:35:18.840
All you're doing now is running away from the troubles in front of you.

00:35:18.840 --> 00:35:21.210
But people are going to die!

00:35:21.210 --> 00:35:23.910
What's this "responsibility" that means I have to kill people?

00:35:23.910 --> 00:35:26.850
I can't make up my mind about something like that so easily!

00:35:37.710 --> 00:35:39.670
Don't be so hard on him.

00:35:43.240 --> 00:35:46.810
They have to look at things that way; it's their job.

00:35:54.230 --> 00:35:56.650
Is something the matter, Commander?

00:35:57.190 --> 00:36:00.000
No, I was just thinking that if I had a son of my own,

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.990
I would've experienced these feelings a long time ago.

00:36:06.140 --> 00:36:10.290
I haven't been this close since that field trip we went on in grade school.

00:36:10.290 --> 00:36:15.130
This is the first thing that comes to mind when I hear "Laplace's Box"...

00:36:15.130 --> 00:36:18.520
Latitude, zero. Longitude, zero. Altitude, 200 kilometers.

00:36:18.520 --> 00:36:20.850
The wreckage of Laplace, the prime minister's residence,

00:36:20.850 --> 00:36:23.190
passes that point once a day without fail.

00:36:23.190 --> 00:36:27.070
I don't think we overlooked something that was right under our noses-

00:36:27.070 --> 00:36:30.740
In my day, it had already been removed from the school tour list.

00:36:30.740 --> 00:36:34.230
Captain, Commander, thank you for looking after us.

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:40.230
I won't play nice and say the pleasure was all ours.

00:36:40.230 --> 00:36:42.420
You brought us nothing but trouble.

00:36:42.420 --> 00:36:45.110
We won't be forgetting that face of yours anytime soon.

00:36:46.070 --> 00:36:49.050
I regret that I won't be able to observe the investigation...

00:36:50.540 --> 00:36:53.550
May fortune continue to smile upon you in battle.

00:36:53.550 --> 00:36:55.140
Good day.

00:36:59.380 --> 00:37:02.710
That's odd. He was always so obsessed with the Box.

00:37:03.220 --> 00:37:05.220
In the end, he's just a lackey to the mighty.

00:37:05.220 --> 00:37:09.400
Anaheim will get the investigation results via Staff HQ.

00:37:09.400 --> 00:37:11.310
Do you suppose that's all there is to it?

00:37:12.270 --> 00:37:16.810
It's not normal to entrust the transport of a prisoner to a civilian ship.

00:37:16.810 --> 00:37:21.130
For HQ to okay that, what do you suppose they have in mind for her?

00:37:21.130 --> 00:37:25.240
Their cover story is that Luna II doesn't have the facilities

00:37:25.240 --> 00:37:27.780
to care for a cyber-Newtype.

00:37:28.910 --> 00:37:30.870
RX-0, launching.

00:37:35.410 --> 00:37:37.620
He feels like piloting it now, eh?

00:37:38.830 --> 00:37:43.170
The Nahel Argama is currently positioned in low Earth orbit.

00:37:43.170 --> 00:37:45.520
In principle, it's no different from operating in space,

00:37:45.520 --> 00:37:47.980
but if you don't constantly maintain the prescribed speed,

00:37:47.980 --> 00:37:51.030
you'll get pulled in by gravity in the blink of an eye, so be careful.

00:37:51.030 --> 00:37:52.140
Right.

00:37:53.790 --> 00:37:57.200
When we were told to attack Palau on our own,

00:37:57.200 --> 00:38:00.190
I'll be honest, we were already weary to the bone.

00:38:01.520 --> 00:38:04.610
But then Commander Daguza spoke up.

00:38:04.610 --> 00:38:09.510
He called it a hostage rescue operation. He said we owed you one.

00:38:10.200 --> 00:38:15.720
He's trying to carry out the responsibility that people should have for one another.

00:38:18.830 --> 00:38:19.510
What is it?

00:38:19.510 --> 00:38:20.020
Nothing.

00:38:20.500 --> 00:38:23.630
Do you ever feel uncertainty, Mr. Daguza?

00:38:24.090 --> 00:38:28.140
I'm a cog, a part of a vast machine called the Federation.

00:38:28.140 --> 00:38:30.760
I carry out the duties I'm given, that's all.

00:38:31.260 --> 00:38:33.860
I can't be certain about anything.

00:38:33.860 --> 00:38:36.650
Not even who's my friend and who's my enemy.

00:38:36.650 --> 00:38:40.400
A person like that isn't qualified to pick up a weapon, is he?

00:38:40.400 --> 00:38:42.990
I never wanted to get in this thing ever again.

00:38:42.990 --> 00:38:46.230
Not even if it meant letting him down.

00:38:48.110 --> 00:38:50.160
Think of it this way.

00:38:50.160 --> 00:38:54.380
You have people around you that you have to take responsibility for.

00:38:54.380 --> 00:38:56.370
You mean Takuya and Micott?

00:38:56.370 --> 00:38:58.000
After we get back to Luna II,

00:38:58.000 --> 00:39:02.000
what happens to those two will depend on what we report.

00:39:02.000 --> 00:39:05.150
What that report says will depend on your actions.

00:39:05.150 --> 00:39:07.050
Taking hostages again, huh?

00:39:07.050 --> 00:39:08.890
Take it however you want.

00:39:08.890 --> 00:39:11.970
You're in a position to be able to alter their fates.

00:39:11.970 --> 00:39:16.470
In that sense, right here and now, you're making the right choice.

00:39:18.060 --> 00:39:19.980
Another launch confirmed.

00:39:19.980 --> 00:39:23.120
It seems to be on a rendezvous trajectory with the suits that launched earlier.

00:39:23.120 --> 00:39:24.820
Is it that Gundam?

00:39:24.820 --> 00:39:27.960
Unable to confirm. No response on psycho-monitor.

00:39:27.960 --> 00:39:31.070
So we can't trace it in its one-horn configuration, huh?

00:39:31.570 --> 00:39:33.540
Status of the Foundation ship?

00:39:33.540 --> 00:39:35.420
On a contact course.

00:39:35.420 --> 00:39:39.080
Assuming the Mock Trojan Horse decelerates to orbital velocity,

00:39:39.750 --> 00:39:42.390
estimated time to contact is approximately ten minutes.

00:39:42.390 --> 00:39:46.340
360 km directly above the equator. East longitude 15 degrees, 28 minutes.

00:39:46.800 --> 00:39:50.390
Just as you've heard it. It looks like their plan is to rendezvous

00:39:50.390 --> 00:39:53.510
and then inspect the designated coordinates.

00:39:53.510 --> 00:39:57.390
Our opening will come when their suits are away at the Laplace wreckage.

00:39:57.370 --> 00:39:58.730
Roger that.

00:39:58.730 --> 00:40:02.040
The Garencieres Team has finally gotten a job that's up its alley.

00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:06.080
Don't get too ambitious. Remember, you have a family waiting at home.

00:40:06.080 --> 00:40:10.570
I understand. I'll bring Marida back safe and sound, don't you worry.

00:40:10.570 --> 00:40:11.920
I'm counting on you.

00:40:14.570 --> 00:40:17.960
It's possible that the La+ Program displays data

00:40:17.960 --> 00:40:20.080
when it recognizes the suit's coordinates.

00:40:20.450 --> 00:40:24.960
The last time the NT-D activated, it didn't display any new information.

00:40:25.710 --> 00:40:30.340
The station wreckage crosses those coordinates every day at 0000 exactly.

00:40:30.800 --> 00:40:34.260
The prime minister's residence that was destroyed by terrorists a long time ago.

00:40:34.260 --> 00:40:37.440
If the Box was hidden in such an obvious place,

00:40:37.440 --> 00:40:40.950
wouldn't somebody have come to check it out long ago?

00:40:40.950 --> 00:40:42.820
We don't know, which is why we're checking it out.

00:40:42.820 --> 00:40:46.440
Focus on your piloting. We'll only get one chance to make contact.

00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:11.810
Conroy, report in if there are any changes, no matter how trivial.

00:41:11.810 --> 00:41:12.650
Roger.

00:41:12.650 --> 00:41:14.880
T-minus 2 minutes to arrival at designated coordinates!

00:41:15.680 --> 00:41:18.320
To save this world from the brink,

00:41:18.320 --> 00:41:21.240
a massive space settlement plan was essential.

00:41:21.240 --> 00:41:27.150
And to carry it out, we needed an arbiter that was on par with God.

00:41:27.150 --> 00:41:29.150
And that was the Federation Government?

00:41:29.150 --> 00:41:32.820
A merciless God that would ruthlessly crush anyone who dared oppose it.

00:41:32.820 --> 00:41:35.110
The station sabotage was the best thing

00:41:35.110 --> 00:41:37.780
that could have happened for the Federation Government.

00:41:37.780 --> 00:41:42.200
It kept its authority under the pretext of terrorism prevention, you see.

00:41:42.870 --> 00:41:46.630
You make it sound like the Federation staged the attack itself.

00:41:46.630 --> 00:41:50.460
In the grownup world, things like that happen sometimes.

00:41:50.460 --> 00:41:53.890
There isn't anyone involved then who is alive now.

00:41:53.890 --> 00:41:58.090
All that survives is the tradition that commands us to fear the Box,

00:41:58.090 --> 00:42:00.810
and the symbiotic relationship with the Vist Foundation,

00:42:00.810 --> 00:42:02.850
which has been preserved because of that.

00:42:02.850 --> 00:42:04.350
Tradition...

00:42:04.350 --> 00:42:06.740
It can't be changed by one person acting alone,

00:42:06.740 --> 00:42:09.620
and no one even feels the slightest bit of aspiration to change it.

00:42:09.620 --> 00:42:11.790
It happens with any organization.

00:42:11.790 --> 00:42:14.490
But, you can't call the cogs in the machine evil, either,

00:42:14.490 --> 00:42:19.030
not when they've only been swallowed by the instinct to maintain the status quo.

00:42:19.030 --> 00:42:23.910
All the Box had to do was stay put these hundred years.

00:42:24.680 --> 00:42:27.410
T-minus 15 seconds to arrival at designated coordinates.

00:42:27.920 --> 00:42:28.830
12...

00:42:28.830 --> 00:42:29.800
11...

00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:30.840
10...

00:42:30.840 --> 00:42:31.840
9...

00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:32.770
8...

00:42:32.770 --> 00:42:33.720
7...

00:42:33.720 --> 00:42:34.670
6...

00:42:34.670 --> 00:42:35.720
5...

00:42:35.720 --> 00:42:36.730
4...

00:42:36.730 --> 00:42:37.680
3...

00:42:37.680 --> 00:42:38.600
2...

00:42:38.600 --> 00:42:39.730
1!

00:42:39.730 --> 00:42:43.300
Zero point has been achieved! Crossing designated coordinates!

00:42:43.760 --> 00:42:46.820
Suit systems nominal. How does it look?

00:42:46.820 --> 00:42:48.690
What? Nothing's happening.

00:42:48.690 --> 00:42:49.710
Any changes on the outside?

00:42:49.710 --> 00:42:53.690
All green. No changes in either Unicorn or Laplace Station wreckage.

00:43:01.450 --> 00:43:05.600
Greetings, citizens of Earth and space.

00:43:05.950 --> 00:43:07.050
Where's that coming from?

00:43:07.050 --> 00:43:08.300
What is this?

00:43:08.300 --> 00:43:11.350
Unknown! Can you pinpoint the transmission origin from your end?

00:43:11.350 --> 00:43:16.010
Radio waves are emanating from the RX-0. Please advise.

00:43:16.010 --> 00:43:16.900
It's coming from here?!

00:43:16.900 --> 00:43:18.420
They're right, no doubt about it.

00:43:19.590 --> 00:43:22.820
I'd like to first express my sincere gratitude for having the opportunity,

00:43:22.820 --> 00:43:26.680
on this momentous occasion, to address all peoples across the Universe.

00:43:31.620 --> 00:43:34.110
The source of the signal is the Unicorn?!

00:43:34.110 --> 00:43:37.380
Was the seal broken when it came into contact with the wreckage?

00:43:37.380 --> 00:43:39.780
What's the status of the NT-D?

00:43:39.780 --> 00:43:42.240
I'm told that its activation has not been observed.

00:43:42.240 --> 00:43:45.810
Orders, sir? Shall I delay our departure so you can watch the investigation?

00:43:45.810 --> 00:43:47.910
Tell the klimt that our departure time

00:43:47.910 --> 00:43:50.750
might have to be changed as circumstances warrant.

00:43:51.210 --> 00:43:53.830
Mas...ter...

00:43:53.830 --> 00:43:55.400
Minovsky particles?!

00:43:55.400 --> 00:43:57.760
Density is rapidly increasing.

00:43:57.760 --> 00:43:59.610
Unable to pinpoint source direction!

00:43:59.610 --> 00:44:01.840
Dispersal pattern is not normalizing!

00:44:02.260 --> 00:44:05.510
Prepare for anti-air combat! All hands, put on normal suits!

00:44:05.890 --> 00:44:09.520
There's a chance that the enemy is mixed in with nearby civilian ships!

00:44:09.520 --> 00:44:11.570
Maintain strict anti-air surveillance!

00:44:11.570 --> 00:44:14.270
Even if that's the case, we're inside Earth's Absolute Defense Zone.

00:44:14.270 --> 00:44:18.000
Camouflaged or no, it's unlikely that they could have snuck in a fleet-scale force.

00:44:18.000 --> 00:44:20.000
That's the problem!

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:24.880
If they're using a small force, it means they have a plan to put them to good use.

00:44:24.880 --> 00:44:28.380
...solutions for these problems,

00:44:28.380 --> 00:44:32.710
and each and every one of us must be willing to change our way of thinking.

00:44:33.710 --> 00:44:37.790
To identify with humanity as a species,

00:44:48.470 --> 00:44:49.280
Commander!

00:44:49.280 --> 00:44:50.720
Banagher!

00:44:50.720 --> 00:44:53.520
Something's coming. The Nahel Argama is being targeted.

00:44:53.980 --> 00:44:55.480
Recall the investigation team!

00:44:55.480 --> 00:44:58.110
We should be able to use the ECOAS Lotos as makeshift gun turrets, too.

00:44:58.080 --> 00:45:00.150
Yes, sir! What about the Unicorn?

00:45:00.150 --> 00:45:02.990
It's piping out some crazy speech.

00:45:02.990 --> 00:45:05.170
Have it evacuate before it becomes a target.

00:45:05.170 --> 00:45:08.580
Roger that. Bridge to all mobile suits.

00:45:08.580 --> 00:45:11.740
Abandon current missions and return to ship immediately!

00:45:13.120 --> 00:45:14.620
What are you...

00:45:15.580 --> 00:45:16.390
Here it comes!

00:45:16.390 --> 00:45:17.880
Can you tell how many?

00:45:17.880 --> 00:45:22.380
One. No, there's another formation following behind it.

00:45:30.970 --> 00:45:34.690
The enemy squadron is pinned down near the station wreckage.

00:45:34.690 --> 00:45:37.730
Good. Gilboa, when you feel it's time to get out, you get out.

00:45:37.730 --> 00:45:38.650
Roger that.

00:45:38.620 --> 00:45:41.860
Watch yourself. That Gundam is moving faster than we thought.

00:45:41.860 --> 00:45:45.200
It looks like it's the only suit that left the wreckage.

00:45:45.200 --> 00:45:47.340
The kid did seem to have good intuition.

00:45:47.340 --> 00:45:49.670
This is bothering me, though.

00:45:49.670 --> 00:45:52.870
You don't think the speech will play and that's it, do you?

00:45:52.870 --> 00:45:55.580
The NT-D isn't active yet.

00:45:55.580 --> 00:45:57.920
There has to be something yet to come that's still hidden.

00:45:57.920 --> 00:45:59.190
Laser signal received!

00:45:59.190 --> 00:46:00.420
From the Rewloola?

00:46:00.420 --> 00:46:02.090
No, not from them. It's-

00:46:02.630 --> 00:46:05.420
Full Frontal... Already here, eh?

00:46:12.010 --> 00:46:14.450
Use your beam magnum! At this range, you can hit him!

00:46:14.450 --> 00:46:16.600
I can't. It's too powerful.

00:46:16.600 --> 00:46:18.190
Is this any time to be holding back?!

00:46:18.190 --> 00:46:19.420
I just need to close in!

00:46:29.570 --> 00:46:31.630
Do you think this is a game, kid?!

00:46:31.630 --> 00:46:33.750
You take out an enemy when you have the chance!

00:46:33.750 --> 00:46:38.870
If you let an enemy go, he might kill an ally or even you !

00:46:38.870 --> 00:46:40.470
Who's playing around?!

00:46:40.470 --> 00:46:43.680
I take it seriously when my life or someone else's is on the line,

00:46:43.680 --> 00:46:45.730
so I'm doing all I can, all right?!

00:46:49.380 --> 00:46:50.720
Stay back, Banagher!

00:46:51.470 --> 00:46:52.470
Mr. Gilboa!

00:46:52.470 --> 00:46:56.600
We won't destroy the ship. Our objective is to take back Marida.

00:46:56.600 --> 00:46:58.410
You're kidding... But how?

00:46:58.410 --> 00:47:02.440
Look, just stay away. There's no need for you to die here.

00:47:02.440 --> 00:47:04.650
Mr. Gilboa, wait!

00:47:04.650 --> 00:47:06.490
Take back the prisoner?

00:47:06.490 --> 00:47:09.450
RX-0 to Romeo 010, request relay.

00:47:09.450 --> 00:47:12.240
Enemy objective appears to be retrieval of prisoner.

00:47:13.580 --> 00:47:14.490
Reinforcements?

00:47:14.490 --> 00:47:15.950
The Red Comet...

00:47:21.170 --> 00:47:24.210
Leave the Mock Trojan Horse to the Garencieres Team.

00:47:24.750 --> 00:47:28.440
As for us, we will attack the Unicorn and trigger the NT-D.

00:47:28.440 --> 00:47:29.230
Yes, sir!

00:47:29.230 --> 00:47:30.440
Don't hold back.

00:47:30.440 --> 00:47:33.140
You can't beat the Gundam unless you fully intend to shoot it down.

00:47:33.140 --> 00:47:36.510
We guards will clear a path for you, sir!

00:47:48.170 --> 00:47:52.700
He's toying with us! As if that attitude will work on us now!

00:47:52.700 --> 00:47:55.030
Come on, let's see you turn into a Gundam!

00:47:56.410 --> 00:47:58.090
Return fire! Aim properly!

00:47:58.090 --> 00:47:59.580
I am!

00:48:03.580 --> 00:48:04.970
Isn't the investigation team back yet?!

00:48:04.970 --> 00:48:08.550
There was a delay in reeling in the Lotos. Five minutes to arrival!

00:48:09.730 --> 00:48:15.010
It's no use, postpone the shuttle departure! We have to take shelter!

00:48:15.010 --> 00:48:17.320
The battle's already begun! We have to get off this ship!

00:48:17.990 --> 00:48:19.240
Hey, the prisoner is awake!

00:48:49.090 --> 00:48:50.720
Fight like you mean it, Banagher!

00:48:50.720 --> 00:48:53.810
If you face off against him, the NT-D should activate.

00:48:53.810 --> 00:48:56.050
If you keep this up, they'll kill us by inches.

00:48:56.050 --> 00:48:58.890
B-But if I go all-out, you'll be...

00:48:58.890 --> 00:49:01.940
The jump seat is fragile, but I'm pretty tough.

00:49:01.940 --> 00:49:04.850
It'd be better to just hand over the machine.

00:49:04.850 --> 00:49:07.440
What do you think will happen to the Nahel Argama without the Unicorn?

00:49:08.710 --> 00:49:10.780
Those people are combat pros.

00:49:10.780 --> 00:49:14.280
If they retrieve the prisoner, they won't pass up a chance to take out an enemy.

00:49:14.280 --> 00:49:16.130
Your friends are on board that ship, too.

00:49:16.490 --> 00:49:19.050
I know that! Believe me, I know!

00:49:19.050 --> 00:49:21.010
I know that, but I still...

00:49:31.050 --> 00:49:32.670
Open the hatch.

00:49:34.470 --> 00:49:35.840
Hurry!

00:49:36.680 --> 00:49:37.610
What are you doing?

00:49:38.700 --> 00:49:40.100
This will let you fight, won't it?

00:49:40.100 --> 00:49:43.830
No... You've got it all wrong. That's not what the problem is! I...

00:49:43.830 --> 00:49:48.270
Banagher, I saw the NT-D start to engage earlier.

00:49:48.810 --> 00:49:51.940
It looked as if it was reacting to you personally.

00:49:51.940 --> 00:49:54.320
To your heart, which sensed something

00:49:54.320 --> 00:49:56.670
as you were listening to the voice of this ghost of Laplace.

00:49:56.670 --> 00:49:59.030
My heart?

00:49:59.030 --> 00:50:02.160
It's not a killing machine that was designed to eradicate Zeon.

00:50:02.160 --> 00:50:06.390
Something else entirely is also incorporated into the Unicorn.

00:50:06.390 --> 00:50:11.210
And that thing is probably controlled by a human heart.

00:50:11.710 --> 00:50:14.940
That might be what the La+ Program really is.

00:50:14.940 --> 00:50:18.720
A guidepost that tests the pilot's heart as it leads him to the Box...

00:50:19.260 --> 00:50:22.520
Whoever built this thing was one devious customer.

00:50:22.520 --> 00:50:24.270
What do you...

00:50:24.270 --> 00:50:25.860
There's no time.

00:50:25.860 --> 00:50:29.410
Once I go outside, you move further in and wait for my signal.

00:50:29.410 --> 00:50:31.310
What are you planning?

00:50:31.310 --> 00:50:35.780
Even a cog in the machine has its pride. You go fulfill your own role.

00:50:35.750 --> 00:50:37.150
My own...

00:50:39.240 --> 00:50:40.780
This knows what it is.

00:50:40.760 --> 00:50:44.370
It's the one part that lets you decide for yourself who you are.

00:50:44.370 --> 00:50:45.720
Don't lose it.

00:50:48.580 --> 00:50:53.160
It is now 23:59, Greenwich Mean Time.

00:50:50.730 --> 00:50:53.160
A responsibility I should carry out...

00:50:54.090 --> 00:50:55.730
It won't be long now.

00:51:11.190 --> 00:51:14.400
...and offer up a prayer.

00:51:15.190 --> 00:51:17.250
All that's left now is the Unicorn.

00:51:17.250 --> 00:51:22.130
May the future of humans in space be a peaceful one.

00:51:22.130 --> 00:51:24.790
It's not out of pride or even to repay a debt.

00:51:24.790 --> 00:51:27.760
I listened to my heart, that's all.

00:51:27.760 --> 00:51:30.120
I guess even cogs have them.

00:51:30.580 --> 00:51:32.130
Hopes.

00:51:30.580 --> 00:51:35.110
...with faith in the god called Possibility.

00:51:42.570 --> 00:51:43.480
He's here!

00:51:43.480 --> 00:51:45.930
Your Vulcans! Potshots are fine, just fire!

00:52:01.800 --> 00:52:03.160
Now!

00:52:07.120 --> 00:52:08.660
Banagher!

00:52:11.830 --> 00:52:13.390
Dagu...

00:52:13.790 --> 00:52:16.290
You're my hope.

00:52:16.290 --> 00:52:18.880
I entrust them all to you, Banagher.

00:52:21.130 --> 00:52:22.630
You killed him!

00:52:43.260 --> 00:52:44.740
Captain!

00:52:47.760 --> 00:52:51.620
It turned into a Gundam! Cuaron, do it just like we planned!

00:52:57.690 --> 00:52:59.630
In the end, he's just an amateur.

00:52:59.630 --> 00:53:02.390
He's behaving exactly like the simulations predicted.

00:53:02.390 --> 00:53:04.380
We'll move in and flank him!

00:53:09.620 --> 00:53:12.700
Feel free to smash anything but the cockpit! Do it!

00:53:22.670 --> 00:53:24.040
We were lured in?!

00:53:24.040 --> 00:53:24.870
Angelo, run!

00:53:24.870 --> 00:53:26.720
He's no ordinary opponent. Disengage!

00:53:30.640 --> 00:53:32.450
You damn monster!

00:53:47.360 --> 00:53:51.030
Captain! Please withdraw! This isn't worth your life!

00:53:54.040 --> 00:53:57.940
Laser contact with Sinanju lost! We can't pick it out from the debris!

00:53:57.940 --> 00:53:59.110
And the Gundam?

00:53:59.110 --> 00:54:00.710
Psycho-monitor still online.

00:54:00.710 --> 00:54:02.860
If we track that, we can get a lock on him.

00:54:02.860 --> 00:54:05.080
Alter heading and trajectory at once.

00:54:05.080 --> 00:54:08.050
We'll retrieve both suits before they're pulled in by the gravity well.

00:54:08.050 --> 00:54:10.080
With me at the helm, sir?

00:54:10.080 --> 00:54:13.620
It's an atmospheric assist maneuver! You'll manage, Flaste!

00:54:13.620 --> 00:54:15.540
Gilboa, time's up.

00:54:15.540 --> 00:54:18.670
You'll never be able to infiltrate the Mock Trojan Horse in this situation.

00:54:19.040 --> 00:54:21.510
But, sir! If we pass up this chance...

00:54:21.510 --> 00:54:22.620
Abort the operation.

00:54:22.620 --> 00:54:26.190
Gilboa Team, redeploy to rescue Frontal Team.

00:54:37.410 --> 00:54:39.850
I'm gonna take you down if nothing else!

00:54:41.020 --> 00:54:43.790
Banagher! If you can hear me, stop this!

00:54:44.480 --> 00:54:47.490
If we keep this up, we'll both burn up in the atmosphere!

00:55:00.920 --> 00:55:02.290
I won't miss this time!

00:55:08.110 --> 00:55:09.360
Banagher!

00:55:18.020 --> 00:55:22.020
Tikva... Look after the family...

00:55:22.730 --> 00:55:24.730
Mr. Gilboa...

00:55:49.350 --> 00:55:58.740
<i>Ano hi fure ta kimi no hitomi ni kuzure ochita</i>

00:55:49.350 --> 00:55:58.740
<i>It collapsed the day I looked into your eyes.</i>

00:55:58.990 --> 00:56:04.260
<i>Tozasareta toki no nagare</i>

00:55:58.990 --> 00:56:04.260
<i>It closed the door of time.</i>

00:56:04.720 --> 00:56:19.660
<i>Kitto boku no koe wa dare ni mo todoka nai yo sakebi tsuzukete iru</i>

00:56:04.720 --> 00:56:19.660
<i>I keep shouting, but my voice doesn't reach anyone.</i>

00:56:20.050 --> 00:56:24.220
<i>Kagi wo kaketa tooi memories</i>

00:56:20.050 --> 00:56:24.220
<i>Past memories are sealed.</i>

00:56:23.950 --> 00:56:28.100
<i>Mawaru ka koto hashiri dashita</i>

00:56:23.950 --> 00:56:28.100
<i>Turn around and run past them!</i>

00:56:27.790 --> 00:56:31.490
<i>Kanashimi no kono hoshi ni</i>

00:56:27.790 --> 00:56:31.490
<i>This planet, covered in the sadness of the stars,</i>

00:56:31.190 --> 00:56:35.780
<i>Utsuru yo everlasting love</i>

00:56:31.190 --> 00:56:35.780
<i>seems to be covered in everlasting love.</i>

00:56:35.470 --> 00:56:39.770
<i>Gareki no uzu kobore ochita</i>

00:56:35.470 --> 00:56:39.770
<i>As the vortex of debris falls,</i>

00:56:39.230 --> 00:56:43.570
<i>Namida mirai terashi dasu yo</i>

00:56:39.230 --> 00:56:43.570
<i>I cry out against the future.</i>

00:56:43.180 --> 00:56:50.290
<i>Doko made mo tsuzuku merry-go-round</i>

00:56:43.180 --> 00:56:50.290
<i>Wherever this merry-go-round leads us.</i>

00:56:54.510 --> 00:57:03.940
<i>Yami ni ukabu hikari egakareta prologue</i>

00:56:54.510 --> 00:57:03.940
<i>The prologue of darkness will turn to light.</i>

00:57:04.260 --> 00:57:09.270
<i>Memaguru shiku ugokidasu</i>

00:57:04.260 --> 00:57:09.270
<i>As life begins to move a dizzying speed,</i>

00:57:09.990 --> 00:57:19.400
<i>Konna boku wo kimi wa hitsuyou to shite kureta</i>

00:57:09.990 --> 00:57:19.400
<i>I realize I need you and you need me.</i>

00:57:19.610 --> 00:57:24.680
<i>Hajimete no nukumori</i>

00:57:19.610 --> 00:57:24.680
<i>The warmth of our first meeting.</i>

00:57:25.330 --> 00:57:29.660
<i>Haruka toki wo koete try again</i>

00:57:25.330 --> 00:57:29.660
<i>It's far in the past, so try again.</i>

00:57:29.240 --> 00:57:33.520
<i>Nemuru kokoro ni wo tomoshita</i>

00:57:29.240 --> 00:57:33.520
<i>Your sleeping heart lit something inside me</i>

00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:36.830
<i>Kanashimi ni tsuzumareta</i>

00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:41.150
<i>and I met the sadness of everlasting love.</i>

00:57:36.440 --> 00:57:41.150
<i>Deai yo everlasting love</i>

00:57:40.730 --> 00:57:44.910
<i>Nageki no uzu kobore ochita</i>

00:57:40.730 --> 00:57:44.910
<i>As the vortex of debris falls,</i>

00:57:44.610 --> 00:57:48.760
<i>Namida negai nigiri shimete</i>

00:57:44.610 --> 00:57:48.760
<i>my tears fall as clutch onto hope.</i>

00:57:48.440 --> 00:57:53.530
<i>Habataku mirai e merry-go-round</i>

00:57:48.440 --> 00:57:53.530
<i>As this merry-go-round soars into the future.</i>

00:57:53.240 --> 00:58:01.180
<i>Nan no tame dare no tame kodoku to mukiau no?</i>

00:57:53.240 --> 00:58:01.180
<i>Has anyone had to face such loneliness?</i>

00:58:00.900 --> 00:58:08.850
<i>Deai ya wakare wo ikusen mo kurikaeshi</i>

00:58:00.900 --> 00:58:08.850
<i>From the thousands of hello's and goodbyes,</i>

00:58:08.580 --> 00:58:12.800
<i>Ashita e to tsunaideru</i>

00:58:08.580 --> 00:58:12.800
<i>have they had hope for tomorrow?</i>

00:58:12.420 --> 00:58:16.560
<i>Senaka no hane kakusanaide</i>

00:58:12.420 --> 00:58:16.560
<i>Don't try to hide the wings on your back.</i>

00:58:16.460 --> 00:58:22.600
<i>Kizama re ta sadame shinjite</i>

00:58:16.460 --> 00:58:22.600
<i>And believe in your destiny.</i>

00:58:22.920 --> 00:58:27.130
<i>Kagi wo kaketa tooi memories</i>

00:58:22.920 --> 00:58:27.130
<i>Past memories are sealed.</i>

00:58:26.850 --> 00:58:31.040
<i>Mawaru ka koto hashiri dashita</i>

00:58:26.850 --> 00:58:31.040
<i>Turn around and run past them!</i>

00:58:30.680 --> 00:58:34.450
<i>Kanashimi no kono hoshi ni</i>

00:58:30.680 --> 00:58:34.450
<i>This planet, covered in the sadness of the stars,</i>

00:58:34.070 --> 00:58:38.840
<i>Utsuru yo everlasting love</i>

00:58:34.070 --> 00:58:38.840
<i>seems to be covered in everlasting love.</i>

00:58:38.320 --> 00:58:42.620
<i>Nozomu mono wa hitotsu dake</i>

00:58:38.320 --> 00:58:42.620
<i>My only desire is,</i>

00:58:42.200 --> 00:58:46.490
<i>Moshimo boku ga kiesatte mo</i>

00:58:42.200 --> 00:58:46.490
<i>even if I disappear,</i>

00:58:46.050 --> 00:58:52.780
<i>Kawaranu omoi wo... you stay, I go</i>

00:58:46.050 --> 00:58:52.780
<i>keep living... you stay I go.</i>
